[about]
Title=10 - Conclusion
Intro=What to carry away from the walks, in four sentences, and where to begin.
Setup=Nothing is needed.
Homework=Open the folder you use most and tag three files.

[step]

Say=Four things to carry away. A key is named for a word of its command, so it can be guessed. The semicolon tags, and every command then acts on all of them. Jump finds by name; Keywords finds by everything known. And the Homer Player is the same in every Homer program.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Start in a folder you use every day, tag what you want to move, and move it. The rest follows from that.
